                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Gereh: public relays",
                            "A relay's owner can, by their own choice, open it to everyone, so users with no relay of their own get their messages too. A phone with no relay borrows one or two public relays by itself, only after the relay itself says it is public; nobody but its owner can make it public. News of public relays spreads phone to phone with the official channel. For a relay made before this version, put the new script code in place of the old once.",
                            Icons.Default.Public
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Gereh: the member count and photo of the official channel and group",
                            "Their member count (everyone who used Gereh lately) is estimated phone to phone, within about 2% and without revealing anyone, and spreads over the Google relay too. Nobody's joining or leaving is shown in the official group; only the number changes. Admins can now set the photo of both, and it reaches everyone.",
                            Icons.Default.Groups
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Gereh: reactions, and the official channel and group fixed",
                            "Reactions now work in one-to-one chats, groups, channels and the official channel and group (hold a message, or tap it twice): one per person per message, channel readers too. In the official chats: admins change the name and description and it reaches everyone; a deleted post goes from the other phones too (posts deleted before this version as well); photos and files can be posted there; a new user gets the posts and the member count from their first contact within seconds, not ten minutes later; and the member count updates at once. Google relay: pausing a relay no longer blocks its owner's own messages, opening a paused relay to everyone no longer says the script is old, and the script code survives copying (for a relay made before, put the new code in place of the old once).",
                            Icons.Default.Favorite
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Gereh: group and channel settings",
                            "A group's or channel's description, members' default rights (who may send text, photos, files, links and the rest, who may add members or pin) and deleting a group or channel for everyone work. The rows that need Telegram's server (public link, boosts and colours, stickers, statistics, translation and the like) are hidden.",
                            Icons.Default.Settings
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Russian and Chinese (Русский, 简体中文)",
                            "Two new languages for the whole app and for Gereh, chosen in Settings › App Language; Gereh follows it with «Same as MLMVPN» or takes its own. In this version the menus, buttons and messages are translated (about 5,600 of the app's texts and all of Gereh's own); part of the text inside some pages, and Telegram's original screens in Gereh, are still in English and follow in the next versions.",
                            Icons.Default.Language
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Outline: Shadowmere's keys, tagged and timed",
                            "Outline now also takes every key shadowmere.xyz lists. Shadowmere checks all its keys itself and hands out only the working ones. As the site is filtered in Iran, the app ships with its 186 keys of 2026-10-25 and updates them only through one of the app's tunnels: by themselves whenever Outline connects, and on «Refresh the lists» while any tile's tunnel is on (Outline, V2Ray, WireGuard or any other); with no tunnel on, the app says to turn one on first. Each of these keys carries the «shadowmere» tag in its name and on its row, with the time Shadowmere last updated it and how often it passed. A «Shadowmere» row on the Outline page and a «shadowmere» chip in the server list show them on their own; «Test all shadowmere» (and «Quick test») pings every one of them, and «Connect to the fastest» then connects to the fastest that answered. Nothing is pinged by itself, only when you tap a test.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Newer build tools",
                            "The app is built with AGP 8.13, Kotlin 2.1 and compileSdk 36 (for Gereh's code). targetSdk stays 34, so the VPN behaves as before. The app is larger because of Gereh.",
                            Icons.Default.Build
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Aether core 2.4.0",
                            "The Aether core behind «وارپ», the Aether screen, the exit-country ping and Game Boost is now its developer's 2.4.0: MASQUE connects sooner where the WARP API is filtered (WARP is no longer switched on again at every connect), making a WARP identity also tries Cloudflare edges when the API's own addresses are blocked, the MASQUE scan tries only known working gateways, on every port, and a tunnel that ran for hours reconnects at once to the same server.",
                            Icons.Default.Waves
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Aether: two new ways to connect and to make a WARP identity",
                            "From PattNG: when MASQUE connects over neither HTTP/3 nor HTTP/2, the Aether screen tries the semi-python ClientHello with fragmenting, then the same ClientHello through Xray's tlshello, and keeps the one that connected for that network. Making a WARP identity (for «ماسک», «وایرگارد», «وارپ در وارپ» and «وارپ») tries the same two ways when ECH and the direct way fail, and remembers per network the way that worked.",
                            Icons.Default.Waves
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The app was closed in the background for its CPU use",
                            "Android closed the app in the background when a process (an engine core such as Lantern, Tor or Geph, or a test process) still worked after you left its page with no VPN up (about 80 reports). Now, two minutes after the app goes to the background with no VPN and no foreground service running, those processes end and a scan stops. Nothing is touched while a VPN is connected.",
                            Icons.Default.BatteryAlert
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Freezes on the home screen and a few other pages",
                            "Slow work moved off the main thread: the home tiles' artwork (now decoded at display size), the connection widget's last method, the disconnect command, the traffic file at connect, the app icons of Anti-sanction, NPV's best-config pick, and stopping Game Booster. On slow phones each of these froze the app for nine seconds or more.",
                            Icons.Default.Speed
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "FENIX did not connect on older phones",
                            "Firefox VPN's servers use a certificate from a root (GlobalSign E46/R46) that older Androids (Android 11, for one) do not have, so every connection to them failed on those phones while the same account worked on a newer one. FENIX now carries those two roots itself, next to the phone's own.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Fewer freezes on slow phones",
                            "The connect button of the home widget, disconnecting a tunnel, the home wallpaper, the Scout page and MAE's app icons no longer hold the main thread, and a connect that reached the tunnel service without its configuration no longer closes the app.",
                            Icons.Default.Speed
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A few more crashes",
                            "Devices without the VPN permission dialog (some TV boxes and projectors) now get a message; stopping in the middle of a Lantern or Psiphon check no longer closes the app; Proton on a phone without WebView; URnetwork on Android 7; copying a very large list in the scanner; an incompatible GST core; an Xray core's process dying; and a config name with a «%».",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A few Gereh faults",
                            "The «this part of Gereh is not built yet» flash on opening the official channel and group and their info pages; profile, group and channel photos showing no thumbnail; a new group or channel missing from the list after going back; the line under a contact's name saying «on this Wi-Fi» after a message through the relay; the «colour themes» strip spinning for ever (now the themes and colours built into the app, offline); the day/night button sticking after one use; the empty three-dot button in Settings; the «app icon» section and privacy options with nothing behind them are hidden; and a clear message when a relay's script code on Google has an error.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                    )
                ),
                ChangelogVersion(
                    "Version 1.2.42",
                    listOf(
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Important: the Cloudflare problem is fixed -- one clean-up is needed",
                            "First delete every Worker, every KV namespace and every D1 database in your Cloudflare account (dashboard). Then deploy again from the app, and in the Cloud section press «سنجش این خط» (the «سنجش روش‌ها روی این شبکه» button on the «روش اتصال این شبکه» card).",
                            Icons.Default.Warning
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A widget for every connection method",
                            "Every connection tile of the app (WireGuard, MASQUE, WARP, Psiphon, Tor, Geph, Lantern, FLUX, FENIX, Amnezia, Outline, OpenVPN, V2Ray and the rest) now has a widget for the phone's home screen that looks like it: one tap connects or disconnects that method, and its lamp says whether it is on or connecting. When a method needs something first (an account, a server list), the tap opens its page instead. Add them from Widget Studio, or by long-pressing an empty spot on the home screen › Widgets › MLMVPN.",
                            Icons.Default.Widgets
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Widget Studio",
                            "A new Widget Studio tile: design widgets of your own. Eight looks (Glass, Minimal, Neon, Colorful, Compact, Dark Pro, iOS Style, Wave), the accent and card colours, how much glass, the corners, the connect button's shape, the method and its country, and what it shows (status, live speed, a live chart, the session's usage, time connected). Save as many designs as you like and place them in three sizes; editing a design updates every widget that wears it. Designs are in the main-settings export too.",
                            Icons.Default.Palette
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A connection widget on the app's home screen",
                            "At the top of the app's home screen, like an iPhone widget: the method that is on, its exit country, a live chart of the traffic, this session's usage and a disconnect button. When you are not connected, it connects the last method in one tap. Remove it with «−» while rearranging the icons; Settings › Display or Widget Studio bring it back.",
                            Icons.Default.ViewQuilt
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "«سنجش این خط» finds the way on more lines",
                            "A few seconds' look at the line comes first, and whatever passed there is proven first, then ECH, IPv6 and F&F in that line's order; before, the measurement ran out of time after two or three. The app fetches the ECH key itself and the summary's addresses are always tried. When no Cloudflare way works, WARP (the «WireGuard» tile) and MASQUE (the «MASQUE» tile) are tried too, and the answer names the tile to connect with.",
                            Icons.Default.Radar
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Lantern, a new engine",
                            "A new Lantern tile with the official Lantern 10 core, as on Windows: all traffic or smart mode (Iranian sites go direct, with the phone's own DNS), «فهرست سرور تازه» when the servers stop answering, and the exit country once connected. When your internet cannot reach Lantern the first time, the first list is fetched through WARP and the connection itself stays direct; later connects take a few seconds. It is in MLM Scout and MAE too. 64-bit phones only; a 32-bit phone shows «not available».",
                            Icons.Default.Lightbulb
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "URnetwork, a new engine",
                            "A new URnetwork tile on URnetwork's own official SDK: traffic leaves through several «provider» devices in different countries at once. The first time it shows only URnetwork's terms and a «Create account» button (an account with no email, and a recovery phrase). While connecting, every step and the providers (being checked, connected out of 12) are shown live. The data card shows used, left and the time to the next grant of the free allowance, which is daily and comes again every day at 00:00 UTC. Ad and tracker blocking (off by default), the exit country changed without dropping the tunnel, smart Iran and MTU from the app's settings, and the official app's power-saving mode while battery saver is on. Moving between Wi-Fi and mobile data keeps the providers. In MAE and MLM Scout too. 64-bit phones only.",
                            Icons.Default.Hub
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "NPV, a new section",
                            "A new NPV tile: configs from NPV channels and your own, in one place. Import an npvt, npvs or text file (from the page, or with the phone's «Open with» and share), or paste a link from the clipboard. «بررسی کانفیگ‌های تازه» reads the 100 default Telegram channels, your own channels and public lists -- reaching Telegram directly, through another VPN or through this app's own tunnel -- puts what is new in the «انبار» store and, when you allow it, tests everything and removes the broken ones. Mark the healthy ones and send them to the main page: «اتصال به سریع‌ترین» connects on the app's V2Ray engine and another tap tries the next config; split tunnelling, LAN sharing and the Smart Iran route apply. npvt and npvs files are encrypted with NPV Tunnel's own key: they are kept and opened in NPV Tunnel, not in this app. Fetching files from Telegram by itself needs a Telegram sign-in that is not ready yet; for now a tap opens the post in Telegram. In MLM Scout too.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Search on the home screen, the iPhone way",
                            "Tap the dots under the home screen (or «جستجو» on a board of one page): tiles come first, inside folders and the dock too, by their Persian or English name or the word people use for them; then, under a line, the Settings rows that match, which open on their page with the row lit up. ي/ی, ك/ک, the half-space and Persian or Latin digits all count as the same.",
                            Icons.Default.Search
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Backup and restore",
                            "Settings › «پشتیبان‌گیری و بازگردانی» exports three parts: the main settings; accounts and configs (Cloudflare, WARP, Geph, FENIX, Proton, Windscribe, GitHub, OpenVPN, configs…); and each method's own settings. The file can have a password (AES-256) and is never uploaded: save it on the phone or send it to yourself. Before a restore you see what the file holds and choose «merge» or «replace completely»; the app closes and opens again for a moment, and if anything fails nothing is changed.",
                            Icons.Default.Backup
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MAE: the exit abroad is the central Worker",
                            "Apps that refuse an Iranian address leave through your Cloudflare account's central Worker (the one the panels ride), and MAE makes no Worker of its own any more; its Proxy IP opens Cloudflare-hosted sites too. MAE's old Worker can be removed under Manage, and when the Worker changes the apps are checked once again.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MAE: Gemini and Google Flow only from a fixed server abroad",
                            "These two open only from one fixed server abroad, so MAE no longer shows them «ready» on the Worker or Lantern, and says so when there is no way. New fixed exits: FENIX (the chosen country and the US), Outline, Proton and Windscribe, beside foreign configs. Set up any of them (for FENIX, only add its account): MAE takes them by itself and measures which works best for each app. The ones not set up are listed under Manage and on each app's route list with an orange «not set up» line, and named under an app that found no way; one tap opens their tile. The US helper is gone from MAE.",
                            Icons.Default.Public
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MAE: Lantern is one of the ways",
                            "While MAE is connected, a Lantern of its own runs for the apps that need an exit abroad, and MAE measures which apps open through it (off on phones with less than 2.5 GB of memory). «استفاده در MAE» on the Lantern page turns it off.",
                            Icons.Default.AutoAwesome
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Psiphon level with Windows",
                            "Six ways to connect, as on Windows: domain fronting (CDN), clean IP, all protocols, relay through other users, personal Conduit and a proxy server; automatic tries them in turn and remembers the winner. Once connected the server's capacity is measured and a very slow server is replaced, and a live card under the button shows the method, protocol, capacity and drops. Proxy server: your own, or a ready list by country that is tested again right before connecting.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Psiphon clean IPs: the real test ten times faster",
                            "Akamai and Fastly clean IPs are found and tested with a real Psiphon. A one-second pre-check of the data path now comes first, and several tests run at once (as many as the phone's memory allows): in our test 309 IPs took about 7 minutes instead of 70, just as accurately. A progress card shows the counts, the IPs being tested, the time left and «⚡ fastest so far» with «انتخاب»; the list sorts by speed as results come in, scrolling no longer stutters and Stop is instant. A wrong result is fixed too: a dead IP that was reported as connected.",
                            Icons.Default.Bolt
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Outline: many more working servers",
                            "No test without your say-so, and «test all» starts at once. Servers that do not answer directly are tested again from inside WARP: in our test about 180 working servers were found instead of a handful. The 1,500-server cap is gone, and a dead server that no list carries any more is dropped after 3 days; favourites and servers that worked stay.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnLock
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Amnezia without a cap",
                            "The 3,000-server cap is gone and opening the page no longer starts a test by itself; a dead server that no list carries any more is dropped after a few days, while your own and the ones that worked stay.",
                            Icons.Default.Storage
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Exit country over IPv4 in WARP, WireGuard and MASQUE",
                            "As on Windows: pick the exit country through an IPv4 proxy (a list of 47,947 proxies in 145 countries ships with the app). Each proxy is tested from inside WARP, the exit country is confirmed after connecting, and a proxy that stops working is replaced by the next one by itself. NAT64 and IPv4 are never on at the same time.",
                            Icons.Default.Language
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MASQUE did not connect? WireGuard",
                            "When MASQUE does not connect in 30 seconds, WireGuard connects by itself and a card says which one you are on; the exit country stays the same. On that network MASQUE does not hold you up again for 12 hours.",
                            Icons.Default.SwapHoriz
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "IPv6 exit country: no more «connected» with nothing coming in",
                            "Sometimes a country's gateway (the Netherlands, in our test) answers the handshake and then brings nothing back, and WireGuard and MASQUE stayed «connected» with 0 B received for two minutes. Now, if nothing comes back within 15 seconds of connecting, the country's next gateway is tried, and a country with no working gateway is not shown as connected. «Fastest country» no longer goes by the ping alone: a country whose ping could not carry the download comes after every one that could (in our test Germany was twice as fast as the United Kingdom it used to pick), and the country list is sorted the same way.",
                            Icons.Default.NetworkCheck
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The app's own update no longer starts over",
                            "The in-app update download was cut after about 95 seconds wherever it had got to (the middle, or near the end) and began again from zero the next time; on most lines it could never finish. That ceiling is gone, what has arrived is kept, and after a dropped connection or the app being closed the download continues from where it stopped; drops are retried by themselves, and the file goes to the installer only when its size and digest match the published release. Store downloads too. The release notes no longer show ## and ** marks.",
                            Icons.Default.Download
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The top crash of 1.2.41 is fixed at its root",
                            "The app closed by itself on connect, disconnect and tests (Outline, Windscribe, Amnezia, MAE, FLUX, the node list, Quick Connect). Xray now runs in a process of its own: a crash there ends only that process, the app stays open and the VPN reconnects by itself.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Freezes and «app not responding» fixed",
                            "The node list with big lists, free configs, the scanner's combine, Quick Connect, Smart Iran's app icons, Proton, Geph, Tor bridges, FLUX countries and the home tiles: the heavy work is off the main thread.",
                            Icons.Default.Speed
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Out of memory with many configs fixed",
                            "The config list is stored in a file of its own, a node at a time (with a backup); the SNI config list shows a page at a time; weak phones skip the heavy decorative fades.",
                            Icons.Default.Memory
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Psiphon, WireGuard and Tor crashes (tun2socks) fixed",
                            "The tun2socks library had been built with debug assertions and closed the app at the smallest mismatch; it is rebuilt properly.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Telegram bridge, MLM Scout and tunnel crashes fixed",
                            "The background services now answer every start request in time.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Phones and TV boxes without a browser or a file picker",
                            "Windscribe sign-up, OpenVPN file import and the FENIX and Proton pages no longer crash; they show a short message.",
                            Icons.Default.Info
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Smaller crashes fixed",
                            "OpenVPN account choice, the network list, the Quick Settings tile, the scanner, VPN permission after leaving a screen, the Android TV remote, running out of threads.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Killed in the background fixed",
                            "The system killed the app for CPU use in the background; no core stays in the app any more and Geph's helper engine stops when you leave its screen.",
                            Icons.Default.Speed
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "More honest crash reports",
                            "Short slow moments are no longer freezes (9 s and up only), and by-design exits of helper processes or memory reclaim by the system are not reported as crashes.",
                            Icons.Default.Info
                        )
                    )
                ),
                ChangelogVersion(
                    "Version 1.2.41",
                    listOf(
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The central Worker: one Worker for every panel, shared with Windows",
                            "Each Cloudflare account has ONE Worker: BPB is the Worker itself and Edge, Zeus, Spider, Netra, Gozargah, Nova, Nahan and MLM each take only a fresh id on the same one — a panel that is not installed no longer gets a Worker or panel code of its own. The id and the settings are kept in the account's shared registry, so a Worker made on Windows shows up here and the other way round; a second Worker is never made and one device's upload never revokes the other's live id. A panel already installed as a full panel keeps its own row. MLM on the phone is Config Studio's engine: connecting it to the central Worker is separate, and its full install is one tap away. The settings (ports, clean IPs, IPv6, ECH and F&F configs, the backup address) are shared between the two devices too.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The connection method for this network, above the Cloudflare chart",
                            "A new card above the usage chart: one button measures which way of reaching Cloudflare works on THIS network (unchanged, ECH, F&F or IPv6), the result is kept for the network, and from then on the scanner, the connect, the health tests and the combined configs use it. The configs the central Worker makes carry ECH and F&F ready; links that name the handshake presets (`semi-python` and `tlshello-0-len`, as on Windows) now work on the phone too.",
                            Icons.Default.Speed
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Deploying and taking configs: direct, and through a tunnel when Cloudflare is blocked",
                            "Direct first, always. Only if Cloudflare is blocked on your line and the direct connection fails, turn on one of the app's tunnels (Psiphon, Tor, Lantern, Geph, the GitHub tunnel or V2Ray) and the same request goes through it, with the name resolved inside the tunnel. While a tunnel is on, a direct connect gives up sooner so a blocked line does not wait a minute. If nothing works the message says exactly what to do. It covers the central Worker, the shared registry, Spider, Netra, Gozargah, Nova, Nahan, MLM and Config Studio.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Telegram Proxy, a new home tile",
                            "Telegram's official «WEB proxy» on a Worker or on Pages of your own Cloudflare account (Telegram for Android 12.10+). One tap builds it, a real question to a Telegram data centre tests it (once through the app's route, once through the phone's own network), and one more tap adds it to Telegram. Up to three proxies per method; state, re-check, cancel, resume of an unfinished build, and delete from Cloudflare. A custom domain of your own with a five-step guide that ticks itself, for networks that block workers.dev. A steady connection: several sockets, a silent switch before one fills up, and a ping every 20 seconds, so «connecting to proxy» no longer keeps coming back; a proxy built earlier updates itself when the tile is opened. A plain MTProto proxy and the sponsor channel cannot run on Cloudflare.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Support the app",
                            "A «Support» button beside the shield on the home screen and «Support us» in About open the donation page in the phone's own browser.",
                            Icons.Default.Favorite
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Telegram Proxy: a bridge with a clean IP",
                            "«Bridge with a clean IP» on a ready proxy: a plain MTProxy on the phone carries Telegram to your proxy through the cleanest Cloudflare IP. The IPs come from the app's own scanner and this network's working edges, and each one is really tested. Telegram's add-proxy sheet opens by itself and a notification keeps the bridge running. Works with any Telegram that supports MTProxy, also where workers.dev is blocked.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The Cloudflare key is no longer shown",
                            "The Global API Key field in the add-account form shows dots and uses the password keyboard; pasting still works.",
                            Icons.Default.Lock
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MLM Scout faster and more accurate",
                            "WARP, MASQUE and WireGuard start from the last working server; working methods are not connected again; Tor has two results, Bridges and Base, and says which way connected.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "App no longer closes when the VPN stops",
                            "Fixed the Xray core's crash when WireGuard connections with junk packets stop (Amnezia, Proton, Windscribe); Amnezia's test all is faster.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MLM Scout reads the line right",
                            "IPv4, IPv6, UDP, the line's delay and direct speed are measured correctly.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Windscribe captcha readable",
                            "The code is drawn as a picture; a wrong answer brings a fresh code, and a New code button asks for another.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Amnezia test all is smooth",
                            "Results come in from the start and Stop works at once.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Smart Iran routing lighter and smarter",
                            "It no longer heats the phone, and any site hosted on an Iranian server is recognised by its address.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Config tests no longer crash the app",
                            "Delay tests and the WARP route of Windscribe and Outline run in separate processes; an Xray panic no longer closes the app. Crashes that were never sent are reported now.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Route chips on every method",
                            "Split tunnel, Local network sharing and Smart Iran routing show on every method's page.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MTU for every method",
                            "Amnezia, Proton, Windscribe, Outline, FLUX, FENIX, MAE, GitHub, GST, anti-sanction, OpenVPN and Geph have their own MTU field.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Outline through WARP",
                            "Outline servers the line drops are now tested and connected from inside Cloudflare WARP, the trick that brought Windscribe, Proton and Amnezia back.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "WireGuard steady with Local network sharing",
                            "With Local network sharing on, WireGuard, MASQUE and WARP-in-WARP dropped every 3 seconds because their local port was taken; a free port is used now.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The identity is kept after a disconnect",
                            "The WireGuard, WARP-in-WARP and MASQUE identity was never deleted and is reused on the next connect; the screen now shows it as made after a disconnect too.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Local network sees every tunnel",
                            "The Local network screen no longer says no tunnel is running with WARP, Geph, Tor, Psiphon or Amnezia up.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Freezes",
                            "A deadlock that froze the app for up to 5 s whenever a test process ended is fixed.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The LAN screen",
                            "It no longer shows a tunnel as on when none is.",
                            Icons.Default.Wifi
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The operator is named right",
                            "On dual-SIM phones the calling SIM's operator was shown instead of the data SIM's (MCI as Irancell and back); now always the SIM that carries data.",
                            Icons.Default.SimCard
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The MLMVPN tile with every engine",
                            "The Quick Settings tile now knows OpenVPN and every engine, disconnects them properly and brings back the same one.",
                            Icons.Default.PowerSettingsNew
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton and Windscribe with LAN sharing on",
                            "They no longer close the app: WireGuard stays on the separate Amnezia engine and the share uses the app's own SOCKS port; Proton's Cloudflare carrier runs in a process of its own.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton pings only on «Ping all»",
                            "The Amnezia screen's automatic ping no longer pings Proton's or Windscribe's servers, and Proton's page shows only a ping you started with «Ping all».",
                            Icons.Default.Speed
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "WARP with LAN sharing on",
                            "With LAN sharing on, WireGuard with no exit country chosen no longer gives up at 60 s; it waits up to 110 s while it finds an endpoint.",
                            Icons.Default.Wifi
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Crash and freeze reports",
                            "A freeze is reported while it happens, with the code the app is stuck in; every crash names its screen, carries the breadcrumbs and whether split tunnel, the smart Iran route and LAN sharing were on, and is written even out of memory. Each Windscribe connect stage is recorded too.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Windscribe crash fixed, captcha readable",
                            "Opening Windscribe could close the app; fixed. The login captcha is letters drawn with symbols, so copying it pasted a jumble: the copy button is gone and the drawing now fits the dialog, easy to read.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MLM Scout no longer crashes on the Psiphon test",
                            "Scout's Psiphon test now runs in its own process.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Disconnecting Proton no longer freezes the app",
                            "Closing Proton no longer locks the screen.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The WireGuard tab opens without freezing",
                            "The WireGuard tab no longer hangs while it opens.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Outline, a new tile",
                            "Outline VPN keys: free Shadowsocks servers from six public lists rebuilt every hour, and your own keys (ss:// and ssconf://, pasted or from a QR). Tested on your line, fastest first, one tap to connect; a server that carries no data is replaced by the next. Delete with six seconds to undo, stars, countries, speed test and exit IP; split tunneling and LAN sharing apply, and it is in MLM Scout.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Smart Iran Routing",
                            "A new switch in Settings > Network: Iranian sites and apps (banks, Snapp, Divar, Bale, Rubika…) go direct, without the VPN, on every engine. Iranian apps never see the VPN, Iran's IP ranges leave the tunnel, and every .ir domain plus tens of thousands of other Iranian sites open directly. The lists refresh daily.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Split tunneling and LAN sharing on every engine",
                            "With Local Network sharing on, MASQUE/WireGuard/WARP-in-WARP, Amnezia, Proton, Windscribe, MAE, FLUX and FENIX really can be shared (some showed «ready» and carried nothing). VPN Gate and the kill switch now follow split tunneling, and «only these apps» behaves the same on every engine.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MLM Scout really tests every method",
                            "Psiphon, Amnezia, Proton, MAE, Google Script, anti-sanction, SNI and domain fronting are no longer «soon»: each is tested the way it connects. Scout no longer says «does not work» for something one setting away from working: MASQUE three ways and with your manual endpoint, more configs and panel configs, and a closed WARP tile says when it still connects through its sibling. The «قطع» tag on MASQUE is gone.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Domain fronting connects again",
                            "The connect check did not know the phone's fronting certificate, so domain fronting was refused at every connect; fixed, and its setup can no longer erase the other configs. Where the filter defeats the Iran configs' cut-up handshake, domain fronting still opens YouTube, Google, Instagram and Reddit with no server (in Chrome, with the certificate installed once).",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Windscribe connects in Iran",
                            "All five protocols (WireGuard, OpenVPN TCP and UDP, Stealth, WStunnel) go through Cloudflare WARP, end to end with Windscribe, even where its addresses are blocked. «Test every server with every protocol» really measures speed, ping and stability of each combination and shows the best. Long sessions repair themselves, and split tunneling and LAN sharing are followed.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "FLUX tries every way in",
                            "Every connect round now mixes direct servers, Cloudflare plain, Cloudflare with ECH, a cut hello and fragmenting, with your own Cloudflare configs first; the winning method is remembered per network.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Google Apps Script connects properly",
                            "A false \"wrong password\", a 404 from a pasted full URL, and \"healthy relay but no data\" are fixed: one password everywhere, relays with a different password are flagged, and the tunnel takes the fastest Google route that answers.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Every reported crash and freeze fixed",
                            "Out of memory with large config lists, freezes at launch and on the home screen, and crashes in the exit-country ping, FENIX, Amnezia on Android 7 and copying thousands of configs.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MAE no longer drops every minute",
                            "Each finished app check or rotated WARP endpoint rebuilt the whole tunnel and every app dropped. Changes are now switched live, or batched with a gap; a dead route is still fixed at once.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "GitHub Tunnel without Cloudflare",
                            "A GitHub account is all it takes: the cloud server is reached through free relays (localhost.run, srv.us…) and the Cloudflare Worker is optional now. Tested and connected on a raw Iranian line.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "WireGuard connects again",
                            "It made its identity and then never connected: whatever the settings said, its search covered IPv4 alone, slowly, and found nothing on a line whose WARP IPv4 is closed. Now IPv4 and IPv6 both, in «turbo»; on a phone it connected in 4 s.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "WARP identity on filtered internets",
                            "Where making a WARP identity is filtered, MASQUE, WireGuard, WARP-in-WARP and «WARP» register it with the name encrypted (ECH); 2-5 s on a phone.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The three WARP tiles stand in for each other",
                            "If MASQUE, WireGuard or WARP-in-WARP is closed on an internet, the connect goes on through the member that gets through, and that internet remembers it: the next tap connects straight away. If all are closed it says so at once and suggests Quick Connect.",
                            Icons.Default.Layers
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Faster WARP tiles",
                            "The search is «turbo» now: the first endpoint that really carries data. WARP-in-WARP went from 47 s to 7-17 s.",
                            Icons.Default.Bolt
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Amnezia through Cloudflare",
                            "A WireGuard server the line blocks now connects from inside Cloudflare WARP and exits in the server's own country. On an Irancell line: 8 of 40 servers directly, 21 of 40 through Cloudflare; the app makes a WARP identity of its own and remembers the way in for each internet.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Amnezia: WireGuard servers are back in the list",
                            "Hysteria2 servers this engine cannot connect had taken the place of almost every WireGuard server; all WireGuard servers are now kept and tried in «test the best».",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Amnezia: self-signed Hysteria2 servers",
                            "Three in four Hysteria2 servers have a self-signed certificate, and none of them could pass a test until now. The app now reads the server's own certificate and accepts exactly that one; certificate checks stay on. On the phone a server that always failed connected. On a line that drops UDP most of them still do not answer.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton finds the best way by itself",
                            "Every way (IPv6, IPv4, plain WireGuard and your own Cloudflare configs) is tried at once and the first that really carries data stays. Then each way's real speed is measured with a short download and the fastest is remembered for that internet. Switching never drops the connection. On a phone: connected in about 10 s, 16-24 Mbps.",
                            Icons.Default.Bolt
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton without IPv6",
                            "On an internet without IPv6, Proton connects through the app's Cloudflare configs, with the method the Cloudflare Doctor found on that internet.",
                            Icons.Default.Shield
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton is stable",
                            "No more glitches and reconnects after a few minutes: a second connection is always ready, a stall is noticed within seconds and covered without a disconnect, and a way that keeps stalling is replaced by another that works.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton: Ping all servers above the list",
                            "With a progress bar, how many are done out of all, the way being tried and a Stop button.",
                            Icons.Default.Speed
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Cloudflare: the right method for each internet",
                            "The Cloudflare engine recognises the current internet and tries the methods that work there first.",
                            Icons.Default.Tune
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Cloudflare scanner: the health test after Combine",
                            "Combined configs now carry the method the scan proved on this internet; on a phone 20 of 20 passed the health test.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton VPN: the free servers of your own account",
                            "One button: Proton's official page opens inside the app, you sign in or make a free account, and the app takes your account's free WireGuard servers by itself. The password, emailed code and CAPTCHA are entered only on Proton's page; the app never sees them. If Proton is filtered on your line, turn on FLUX, Tor or WireGuard (or any other engine) with one tap as the way in; once you have the servers the app turns it off, pings them and connects to the fastest. It connects through the Amnezia engine, among Proton's servers only. A free account connects one device at a time.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton VPN: the sign-in page no longer stays white",
                            "The page loaded completely but was drawn above the screen, because the app's WebView gave it a viewport height of zero. It shows properly now; FENIX's sign-in pages got the same fix.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton VPN: signing in brings the servers by itself",
                            "No more making a file per server in Proton's dashboard. Once you sign in, the app takes all of your account's free servers itself (111, in 10 countries) with a single key, the way Proton's own dashboard makes them. The password still never reaches the app.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton VPN: connects on filtered lines with Stealth and IPv6",
                            "On a line that filters Proton, plain WireGuard was choked right after its handshake. Every server now connects the way Proton's own apps do there -- Stealth (WireGuard inside TLS on 443), over IPv6 first. On a phone 44 servers answered and it connected to the Netherlands and Canada. The list is sorted fastest first.",
                            Icons.Default.Shield
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton VPN: the right lamp",
                            "While Proton is connected, the home lamp is on Proton's tile, not on Amnezia's.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Proton VPN: steady over a slow way in",
                            "A more patient check, the page reloading itself, cut requests sent again, and the page stays open when the engine drops for a moment. When no Proton server answers (a network that blocks UDP), the reason is now shown.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "FLUX: no more constant disconnects",
                            "It keeps up to three standby routes, so a dying route hands over to the next by itself. The health check is more patient, a failover keeps the tunnel up and switches only to a route that answered, and a search that finds nothing no longer turns the VPN off at once.",
                            Icons.Default.Bolt
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Game Booster: fixed unintended disconnections",
                            "The monitor no longer mistakes healthy Amnezia and FENIX connections for lost routes and disconnects them. Stopping cancels a pending connection; restarting waits for the previous session to finish, and test cleanup does not stop a newer connection or a WARP engine owned by another session.",
                            Icons.Default.SportsEsports
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Game Booster: more accurate readings of the active route",
                            "Live Amnezia and FENIX measurements now follow the selected tunnel. Secure connection setup time is shown separately from ping and is not compared with measurements made by another method. Packet reordering, previously always reported as zero, is counted correctly in both tests and live statistics.",
                            Icons.Default.SportsEsports
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Game Booster: scan budgets and slow DNS handling",
                            "Quick and thorough checks each share a time budget across their stages. Slow DNS no longer holds up the entire check, and a slow region does not erase completed results from other regions. Cancelling closes test connections, and a ready WARP engine is reused for the final connection when possible.",
                            Icons.Default.SportsEsports
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Game Booster: testing tunnels when direct access is blocked",
                            "A test destination blocked on the direct route no longer prevents tunnel testing. If a pinned tunnel fails, the app reports a failure instead of silently falling back to direct access. Saved FENIX accounts are available to the check after a fresh app launch without opening the FENIX screen first.",
                            Icons.Default.SportsEsports
                        ),
                    )
                ),
                ChangelogVersion(
                    "Version 1.2.40",
                    listOf(
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Game Booster: filtered or sanctioned games",
                            "A new switch, «This game is filtered, sanctioned or won't load»: the direct line is never used for it, and the fastest of Amnezia, WireGuard, WARP and FENIX to the game's own server is. WireGuard, Amnezia and FENIX can also be pinned in Advanced.",
                            Icons.Default.SportsEsports
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "SNI anti-filter fixed",
                            "On the new filtering none of the 14 SNI methods carried data: the filter reassembles the split handshake. A new ECH method encrypts the server name instead; on the phone 9 of 9 SNI configs carried data with it. The method that works is remembered, and building SNI configs now sees the configs fetched in Cloud.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnLock
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "WARP-in-WARP and MASQUE: a new tunnel core",
                            "WARP-in-WARP dropped about a minute after connecting when the core crashed; the tunnel core is rebuilt from its newer source and that crash is gone. A WireGuard tunnel is no longer declared dead after 10 quiet seconds. MASQUE is automatic now: HTTP/3 first (port 443 and ports 1701, 8095, 500, 4500), then HTTP/2 with fragmentation; whichever connects is remembered for that network.",
                            Icons.Default.Bolt
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "MLM panel XHTTP",
                            "The MLM panel's installer never sent the Durable Object binding XHTTP needs, so XHTTP carried nothing. It does now; press the MLM panel's Update once (build 24).",
                            Icons.Default.SwapVert
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Iran configs: the test fixed",
                            "The test only called each config's DNS server on its own, so it showed working configs as dead and dead ones as working. Now every config is run for real and opens YouTube through itself: green opened it, orange connects but cannot open filtered sites, red opened nothing. Connecting one also has to open a site before it is shown as connected.",
                            Icons.Default.Speed
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Store: Iran configs from the developer's GitHub",
                            "The store now reads patterniha's files directly (through jsDelivr when GitHub is filtered), builds the nineteen configs on the phone, has the real Xray core start them, and only then installs. The previous list stays for rollback.",
                            Icons.Default.Flag
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Aether 2.3.0, with HTTP/3 or HTTP/2 chosen for you",
                            "MASQUE and gool try HTTP/3, then HTTP/2, then HTTP/2 with fragmenting on their own. Whichever really carried data on a network is remembered and used first next time, without testing; if it stops working, the others are tried again. gool is back on the Aether screen and comes out at a foreign address.",
                            Icons.Default.Bolt
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Cloudflare Doctor: a full audit, faster connects and a look that matches the app",
                            "A connect no longer spends minutes diagnosing first: the proven way is used at once and the tunnel itself confirms it with real data (an exact download and an upload that is echoed back); only if no data moves is another way found and the connect retried once. A tunnel that starts but carries nothing is reported as failed. The scanner scans your own address list and ports again (they could be replaced or dropped, including every IPv6 address), runs in parallel again, and no longer throws away addresses that only work with a special handshake before testing them. A rejected token is no longer blamed on the network route, and the check stops right there. Learning survives Wi-Fi reconnects. Doctor was rebuilt from the app's own iOS pieces; the first-run check never blocks Cloud for someone without an account, and no step turns green without a real test.",
                            Icons.Default.HealthAndSafety
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "76 real ways to reach Cloudflare, and XHTTP over HTTP/2",
                            "A second, non-Google DNS, a cut inside the server name, the ClientHello in two TLS records, a mixed-case server name, TLS 1.3, three Cloudflare address ranges, iOS, Edge and Android fingerprints, more ports, ECH on clean addresses, the WARP identity through your worker without splitting, and the config exactly as written. For XHTTP configs: HTTP/2 or HTTP/1.1, packet-up or stream-up, with or without fragmentation. Each is chosen and saved only after real data has moved on that network.",
                            Icons.Default.AltRoute
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "XHTTP configs from the MLM panel",
                            "A new «Get XHTTP config» row above «Users» in the MLM panel. Panel build 23 hands every request of an XHTTP session to that session's Durable Object, so the uploads and the download finally meet on workers.dev. The config is added only after it carried real data on this network. Panels installed earlier need the Update row first.",
                            Icons.Default.SwapVert
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Cloudflare Doctor and proven routes for each network",
                            "Five setup steps in Cloud cover six independent stages, reuse proven strategies and replace failed ones. Tunnel success requires real data transfer. Seven taps on the About version enable technical details. Retained accounts and identities use encrypted storage.",
                            Icons.Default.HealthAndSafety
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Choose deploy panels in Doctor",
                            "After Doctor proves the Deploy route, it lists BPB, EDG, Nahan, Spider, Netra, Gozargah, Nova and MLM. Pick one, several or none; only selected panels are deployed and each result is shown separately.",
                            Icons.Default.ViewModule
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Choose config panels in Doctor",
                            "After Doctor proves the Config route, it lists the installed panels and lets you fetch configs from one, several or none. Each successful panel is saved as its own Cloud group and failures are shown separately.",
                            Icons.Default.Download
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Adding an account, deploying and fetching configs now work where Cloudflare is filtered by name",
                            "Many people could not even connect their Cloudflare account, deploy a worker or fetch a config, because on their network the names api.cloudflare.com and workers.dev are read in the first TLS packet and dropped. The app's own Cloudflare calls (adding and verifying an account, creating the subdomain, uploading a worker, KV and D1, fetching configs from the panels, and updating workers) now take the same route the rest of the app uses for Cloudflare: a Cloudflare edge address that answers on this network, with the first TLS handshake (the ClientHello) sent in small pieces so the server name is not in one packet for the filter to match. It is the same thing the app already did to fetch a WARP key, now on the account, deploy and config paths too. Where Cloudflare was reachable already, nothing changes. No new library, no increase in app size.",
                            Icons.Default.CloudDone
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Cloudflare connectivity optimization, on by default",
                            "Automatic changes use a strategy proven for the current network and stage. Fragment is not applied universally. A fresh failure revokes the saved winner and triggers fallback. Explicit link settings remain supported.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Real validation for each Cloudflare stage",
                            "Account and identity, creating a nonce test Worker and deleting it, fetching usable configs, scanning and transferring data through the tunnel are checked separately. Missing accounts or configs are reported as unmet prerequisites. Legacy diagnostics are available in developer mode.",
                            Icons.Default.MedicalServices
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Steadier Cloudflare connections in every region",
                            "The Doctor reports showed some Cloudflare addresses working in one Iranian region and dead in the next, and the phone's DNS sometimes handing out a dead or bogus one. The app now checks a few Cloudflare addresses per network in about three seconds and uses one that answers -- for the Cloudflare account, the panels, WARP registration, and configs whose address does not answer on this network (same worker, another address). Addresses the scanner finds join that list.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Stability: reported crashes fixed",
                            "From the automatic crash reports: the crash when the app was in the background and the network dropped and came back (half of all reports), Android 7 crashes, the Config Studio install crash on a weak connection, bulk tests crashing old phones, freezes at app start and on Tor's screen, the home screen crashing on a very large wallpaper photo, and several smaller crashes.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Tor: bridge management",
                            "A new Bridges row on Tor's screen, beside Connection mode and Exit country. Automatic takes the best tested bridges from Tor's official service (Moat) and three bridge collectors, drops duplicates and dead ones, refreshes itself every few hours, and ranks first the bridges Tor really connected through. The list shows country (flag and name), kind and “Working · 187 ms”, with single and bulk tests, sorting, and manual bridges with clear errors; plus new WebTunnel and plain-bridge modes. About 260 working bridges ship with the app for the first run; the list grows with every refresh; bridges are grouped by country; “Connect through this bridge” picks one by hand; and “Remove down bridges” clears the dead ones in one tap. Once Tor connects, the bridge's country (the way in) is shown beside the exit country, with a word on why they can differ and how to pick an exit country or the fastest bridge.",
                            Icons.Default.Hub
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Store: no version shown for Xray, Psiphon and AmneziaWG",
                            "The version in use and the developer's newest on its own GitHub (XTLS, Psiphon, AmneziaWG) are now shown. These three are built into the app and update with it. AmneziaWG's source now points at the library the app actually uses.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Store: downloads pause and resume",
                            "Downloads can be paused and resumed and continue where they stopped, not from the start. If the connection drops mid-download, it retries three times from the same point before trying the next mirror. Progress reads “12 of 45 MB · 1.2 MB/s · 20 s left”, and Cancel download is separate.",
                            Icons.Default.Download
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Geph: the country test results vanished after connecting",
                            "The last run now stays, with every country and its numbers, says how long ago it was measured, and offers Measure again.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Geph: the country test said “no answer” for every country",
                            "Each country had only 30 s (the real connection has 120 s) and was tested over a different path from the real connection. Now each gets up to 90 s and is checked exactly as the real connection is, a failed download no longer marks a working country as dead, and a country that fails says why. The speed test file changed too: through Geph's exits Google answered the old one with 404, so the speed figure meant nothing.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Geph: connects without making an account by hand",
                            "Connect used to say “make an account first”. Now, with no account, the app makes a free Geph account itself (no e-mail or password; first time only, usually a minute or two) and then connects. The account code is on Geph's account page as before.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "FENIX: several accounts, and one-button sign-in or sign-up",
                            "Add as many Firefox accounts as you like. Each connection takes the next account in turn, checked first to really work and have data left; if an account runs out while connected, the tunnel moves to the next by itself. The Accounts page shows each account's email, data left and refill date. The 50 GB limit is monthly. One button, Sign in or create an account: Mozilla's own page opens in the app, you sign in or sign up with email or Continue with Google, and the account is added on its own at the end; once per account, and the password never passes through the app.",
                            Icons.Default.People
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "FENIX: data left never moved",
                            "“50 of 50 GB” was only read when connecting. It now refreshes when the screen opens, every 3 minutes while connected and from the refresh button, and shows the refill date.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "FENIX: Firefox's free VPN",
                            "A new tile: Mozilla's servers in 33 countries, 50 GB a month free, on your own Firefox account. One-tap account creation in the app, ping every country, fastest country, data left, fast connections on one HTTP/2 session with a standby path, and no DNS, IPv6 or UDP leaks. MAE uses it as a foreign exit too.",
                            Icons.Default.LocalFireDepartment
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Exit country in WARP, MASQUE and WireGuard",
                            "A new Exit country row with flags and names. The tunnel comes out in the chosen country (Netherlands, UK, Germany, Finland, US, Hong Kong and more); it needs IPv6 on your line. Direct connection stays the default: an Iranian IP, but filtered sites open.",
                            Icons.Default.Public
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Real ping per country",
                            "Ping every country makes a short real connection through each one and shows ping, speed and the real exit country. Fastest country picks for you, and if a country's server does not answer, its next server is tried.",
                            Icons.Default.NetworkCheck
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Your own NAT64 and config copy",
                            "Add your own NAT64 gateway, and hold a country to copy a WireGuard config that exits there. The country list refreshes daily from public sources.",
                            Icons.Default.Add
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Safe core updates from the store",
                            "A new Aether or tunnel core that does not fit the app is no longer installed; the working one stays.",
                            Icons.Default.Storefront
                        )
                    )
                ),
                ChangelogVersion(
                    "Version 1.2.39",
                    listOf(
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Amnezia: free WireGuard with obfuscation",
                            "A new tile with free WireGuard and Hysteria servers from 11 lists, plus your own .conf files. Real delay like v2ray, countries that follow the real exit after connecting, dead servers removed, and a connect button that waits for a real connection and can be cancelled. 135 working servers ship inside the app.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Cloudflare Doctor",
                            "One check that says where the Cloudflare account, panel configs, config connections and the IP scanner each break, and what works on your internet. Send its report in the mlmvpn group so it can be fixed for everyone.",
                            Icons.Default.HealthAndSafety
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Free OpenVPN files",
                            ".ovpn files with extra options now import, and profiles that carry their own username and password connect without an account.",
                            Icons.Default.FileOpen
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "FLUX over IPv6",
                            "IPv6 mode now finds routes on networks that have IPv6. The Cloudflare check uses the right IPv6 ranges, and servers whose names are filtered are resolved through DoH. The error message is more precise too.",
                            Icons.Default.Public
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "More countries, change while connected",
                            "More countries are listed (unverified ones are marked), and on Wi-Fi FLUX gradually measures where nodes really exit. Country and IP version can now be changed while connected.",
                            Icons.Default.Bolt
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "FLUX now really connects",
                            "When only one healthy route was found, the tunnel did not start and FLUX said no route was found. That is fixed. One broken node no longer takes a whole race down, and a round that finds nothing moves on to fresh nodes, up to three rounds.",
                            Icons.Default.Bolt
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Detailed logs for troubleshooting",
                            "Every FLUX step is logged under the FLUX tag in logcat: sources, the Cloudflare check, each node's result and why it failed, and the tunnel start. No password or UUID is ever written.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "New engine: FLUX — country, IP version, connect",
                            "Pick a country (or Automatic) and IPv4/IPv6/Both, and connect. FLUX chooses the protocol, server, Cloudflare edge, fragmenting and standby routes itself. On a network it has seen, it connects almost at once. A dead route is replaced by a standby in under a second without dropping the VPN. “Connected” is shown only after a real request went through the tunnel.",
                            Icons.Default.Bolt
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Works even where Cloudflare is cut",
                            "FLUX checks on each network whether Cloudflare is reachable. Where it is not, Cloudflare-fronted configs are not tried at all, and only direct routes such as REALITY and Hysteria2 are raced. FLUX's sources are its own, separate from Free Configs and Quick Connect.",
                            Icons.Default.Public
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "No leaks, and the real country",
                            "All DNS goes through the tunnel, and in IPv4 mode Android blocks IPv6 entirely. The exit country is measured through the route itself, from two independent sources, never taken from a server's name. The adaptive engine (MAE) can use FLUX's proven routes too.",
                            Icons.Default.AutoAwesome
                        ),
                    )
                ),
                ChangelogVersion(
                    "Version 1.2.38",
                    listOf(
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Folders on the home screen, the iOS way",
                            "Hold an app over another until a plate grows behind it, and let go: both go into a folder. Hold an app over a folder to open it and place the app exactly where you want inside, or drag it out. While rearranging, folders wear the “−” badge, removing one asks first and the apps go back where it was. The name can be changed, and a folder with more than nine apps pages sideways. Dragging icons was rebuilt too: nothing moves under your finger until it rests.",
                            Icons.Default.Folder
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Crash reports that always reach the developers",
                            "Every crash, whether Java, native or a hang, is now reported and sent with the app version and your last action. Sending is automatic, retried later when there is no internet and even after the phone restarts. The first time it tells you what was sent (only the error and the phone model, never configs or traffic), and you can turn it off in Settings → Crash report. Reports no longer get lost on the pool's busiest days.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Less battery drain while connected",
                            "The VPN service held its wake lock for ever, so the CPU never slept. It is now held only during a connect and during a real transfer while the screen is off. The adaptive engine puts routine re-checks of known networks off until the screen comes on. Screens out of sight and always-on animations no longer run.",
                            Icons.Default.BatteryFull
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "It repairs a broken route by itself",
                            "When an app's route stops working mid-use, the adaptive engine now notices on its own. For example, Instagram's videos would not play after the phone sat idle for about 20 minutes, until you disconnected and reconnected by hand. Every 5 minutes, and whenever you unlock the phone after a few minutes, each app's route is tried from inside the connection itself. A broken route is swapped for the next working one at once, or the engine reconnects once by itself if it has to. The app's row says so.",
                            Icons.Default.Healing
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "TikTok and sanctioned apps through your own Cloudflare configs",
                            "These apps refuse Iranian addresses, and WARP, WARP-in-WARP, WireGuard and MASQUE all give an Iranian address, so they are set aside for them. The engine now takes configs automatically from the panels on your own Cloudflare account (BPB, EDG, MLM, Netra and the others). It tries them on a clean IPv6 address first and on IPv4 if that does not answer, and picks the fastest for each app. On Android 10 and later, all of the app's traffic takes that route, not only its known domains.",
                            Icons.Default.Public
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "“Didn't open” really fixes things",
                            "Every 👎 is now a genuinely different approach, and it sticks. For sanctioned apps it goes straight to a foreign exit the first time. The app's open connections move to the new route, and the next routine check does not undo the repair. Cancelling the “what's wrong?” question no longer wastes a step. What happened is written on the app's own row.",
                            Icons.Default.ThumbsUpDown
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A Cloudflare account first",
                            "The adaptive engine does not run without a Cloudflare account, because its foreign exits are built on it. With no account connected, you connect one right there, and it is added to «Cloud» too.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Adding apps without reconnecting",
                            "Picking other apps no longer reconnects the tunnel on every tap; the changes are applied once when you leave the list. Only the new app is checked, not the whole list. Google's apps such as Maps and Gmail can now be picked.",
                            Icons.Default.AddCircle
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Check again, and iPhone-style swipes",
                            "A “Check all again” button and a check button beside each app were added; pulling the page down checks them all too. Swipe an app's row left for Delete and right for Check again.",
                            Icons.Default.Refresh
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A redesigned app manager",
                            "Each app has its own page: its route as a checkmark list, an on/off switch, Check again, and a red Remove on its own at the bottom that asks first. The SIM and time-zone warning was taken off the app rows.",
                            Icons.Default.Tune
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Exits have version numbers",
                            "The adaptive engine's foreign exit, the US exit for Gemini and the WARP identity worker now have versions. When up to date they are not reinstalled on every tap: only a Reinstall that asks first; a newer version shows a red badge. Reinstalling the exit no longer re-checks every app from scratch.",
                            Icons.Default.NewReleases
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "OpenVPN: real measuring, reliable cancel",
                            "The delay test now goes as far as the server's TLS answer, and a server that answers only the first packet shows as “Blocked”. Measuring runs in parallel, faster, with a progress bar and a count. Connecting to a dead server no longer sticks on “Connecting”: Cancel frees it within 5 seconds, and a server that has not connected within 60 seconds is stopped with a message.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "An iPhone-style update badge",
                            "Instead of the small icon at the top of the screen, a red number now appears on the Settings icon, and a “Software Update Available” row at the top of Settings. The adaptive engine also has a new icon.",
                            Icons.Default.SystemUpdate
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Smarter and more accurate",
                            "Nothing is learned without internet or behind a Wi-Fi login page. A route that failed only for one filtered app is no longer marked broken for all. ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini never leave over an Iranian address on a new network, not even for a moment. Play Store downloads and YouTube images no longer go through the Gemini exit. On dual-SIM phones, the data SIM is the one that counts.",
                            Icons.Default.Speed
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A steadier, safer connection",
                            "Route changes (such as a rotated WARP endpoint or a new Worker) now reach the running connection, and the needless reconnect every 6 hours is gone. WARP no longer interferes with itself. Auto-switch no longer replaces an adaptive-engine session. The Quick Settings tile and the reconnect after a network drop build a fresh config for the current network. The WARP key and the Worker's id are no longer stored for the tile.",
                            Icons.Default.Sync
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A smoother screen",
                            "The adaptive engine's screen no longer stalls when it opens or during checks, and the app list scrolls more smoothly. Routes are named in plain words: Direct, Filter bypass, WARP, Cloud config, with the exit's country flag. Removing an app asks first.",
                            Icons.Default.Apps
                        ),
                    ),
                ),
                ChangelogVersion(
                    "Version 1.2.37",
                    listOf(
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "New engine: MLM Adaptive Engine (experimental)",
                            "Pick the apps and sites you use most; the engine finds the best route for each one on each network: direct, Serverless, WARP or a foreign exit. Each app gets its own route while everything else keeps Serverless speed. “Didn't open” (👎) re-checks it, and from the second time asks what is wrong so every attempt is a different approach. Installed apps can be added too.",
                            Icons.Default.AutoAwesome
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Gemini and Google Flow through the US exit",
                            "Cloudflare configs leave from the Cloudflare centre nearest the phone, which Google places in Iran (error 1060). The adaptive engine sets up the US exit on your own Cloudflare account automatically and sends Gemini and Flow through it, with the rest of the same Google account. Measured on the phone: Gemini answered on Irancell and Flow opened on MCI.",
                            Icons.Default.Public
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Cloudflare keys are safer",
                            "Cloudflare account keys are now encrypted with Android's own secure key, left out of Android backups, and removed from crash reports.",
                            Icons.Default.Lock
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Reconnects after a network drop",
                            "After the internet dropped and came back, the connection sometimes never returned. It now reconnects by itself in about 3 seconds.",
                            Icons.Default.Refresh
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Two Android 8/9 fixes",
                            "The “download error” when installing the Google Script certificate, and OpenVPN closing suddenly on Android 8.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                    ),
                ),
                ChangelogVersion(
                    "Version 1.2.36",
                    listOf(
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "New engine: Geph",
                            "The Geph network is now its own app on the home screen, running Geph's own unmodified engine, whose signature is checked before it is installed. The whole phone goes through the tunnel, IPv6 included, so nothing leaves on your own line. When the network changes or the engine stops, the engine comes back up while the tunnel stays open. It shows \"connected\" only after a real request has crossed the tunnel.\n\nFeatures: a free account or sign-in with an account code, account type and expiry, data left, a new code, free and gift codes, exit country and city, finding the fastest server, a speed test, direct connection to the exit, ad and adult filters, proxy-only mode, port forwarding, LAN sharing, Geph news, and sessions with a live log. There is no purchase in the app.",
                            Icons.Default.Shield
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "New engine: WARP",
                            "Cloudflare's own WARP on an engine separate from MASQUE, WireGuard and WARP-in-WARP, as on Windows. It registers its own WARP account (through your own Worker where Cloudflare's API is filtered) and counts as connected only when Cloudflare says the traffic really went through WARP. If the endpoint stops carrying traffic, it finds another while the tunnel stays open. Its settings cover the search mode, address family, obfuscation and keepalive.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "New engine: OpenVPN with TunnelBear servers",
                            "TunnelBear's servers with your own account, direct, with no other tunnel under them. A round button, a live card with speed and usage, a server page with flags and country names, and an account page, with no pop-ups. It shows \"connected\" only after real data has crossed the tunnel.\n\nEach TunnelBear country name stands for about 20 servers, and some of them do not answer from Iran. The delay test now measures several servers of each country together, and the connection goes to the ones that answered. If one goes silent after the start, the next attempt goes to the next server. Measured on a phone: connected in 4 s, about 11 Mbit/s down.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Config Arena: your cloud panels, racing",
                            "One button in Cloud prepares your panels (BPB, Edge, Nahan, MLM, Spider, Netra and Gozargah), takes a config from each and races them on real measurements: qualifying, latency, reaching Cloudflare-hosted sites, and in Full mode speed and stability. Pit lane, grid reveal, start lights, a live track, a podium and medals. Calm colours in keeping with the app's iOS look, and light sound effects (a beep per light and a long start beep, as on a motor-racing start line; retirement, finish, winner) with a mute button. The result page keeps the podium with the top three and their scores. The winner connects or saves with one tap, and races are kept with their time and network. Installs and updates happen only after one confirmation page; a panel that fails sits out and the others go on. To keep it fair, every race first finds one clean IP and puts it on every panel's config, so the panels are compared rather than their addresses. It is chosen from the scanner and Cloudflare's ranges: steadiness first (5 clean handshakes, least spread), then a real download. It works for an operator who has never scanned too.",
                            Icons.Default.EmojiEvents
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "New Cloud panel: Nova (Nova Proxy)",
                            "The Nova panel installs on your own Cloudflare account with one tap: the code is taken straight from the developer's GitHub and checked against the SHA-256 the developer publishes before it is deployed. The panel is locked at once with a random password, so nobody can claim it before you. «Get configs» takes the panel's full subscription (17 configs on the phone), the combine assistant is offered, and Nova is in the arena and the Store too.\n\nMeasured on the phone: install, the panel locked, and 17 configs fetched.",
                            Icons.Default.AutoAwesome
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The usage chart follows Iran's calendar",
                            "The chart at the top of Cloud shows this week from Saturday to Friday in Tehran time, with the Persian date («Today · Monday 6 Mehr»). Days after today stay empty and the average counts only the days of this week that have passed.",
                            Icons.Default.DateRange
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Latest changes on the update page",
                            "When the app is up to date, «Latest changes» shows the full notes of the latest public release, fetched fresh from GitHub each time; when GitHub cannot be reached, this version's notes from inside the app are shown.",
                            Icons.Default.Info
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Tighter filtering: the app moves itself from IPv4 to IPv6",
                            "Under the tightened filtering, connections to Cloudflare IPv4 opened and then carried no data: panel configs did not answer, the scanner found no IP, config fetches from MLM, Spider, Netra and Gozargah timed out, and GitHub Tunnel stopped. On the same phone Cloudflare IPv6 was open.\n\nThe app now measures which family carries traffic on the current network and uses it:\n• The scanner tests the ranges and IPv6 with a real request first and moves to IPv6 when IPv4 is closed; addresses that complete the handshake and then stay silent are dropped in under a second.\n• Cloudflare-fronted configs (BPB, Edge…) move to a healthy IPv6 address on connect and in delay tests when IPv4 is dead; same Worker, same name.\n• Config fetches from panels check each address with a real request and use a healthy one.\n• GitHub Tunnel, WARP, WireGuard, WARP-in-WARP and MASQUE know IPv6 too.\n• Each Worker's failure reason, from Cloudflare itself, goes to the app's log.\n\nMeasured on the phone: 10 healthy IPs in 26 s, a connection downloading 1 MB in 2–3 s, configs fetched from all 7 panels, and GitHub Tunnel at 2.2 Mbit/s.",
                            Icons.Default.Language
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Cloud: a daily-usage chart and folding accounts",
                            "The Cloud page opens on a daily-usage chart in the style of iPhone Screen Time: today's requests as one big number, seven days of bars stacked by account in each account's colour, an average line, and a bar per account showing how much of that day's free 100,000 it used (orange near the limit, then red). Tap a day to see its figures. With several accounts one card is open and the rest fold to a row that opens with a tap. Each panel has its own coloured icon (as in iPhone Settings) with an Installed, Update or Not installed label, and the rows sit on the card instead of a dark strip. Every account's received configs are one module below the accounts, with the panel's icon and the account's colour. Nothing was removed from the page.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Two new Cloud panels: Netra and Gozargah",
                            "Netra (built on BPB) and Gozargah (multi-user, on D1) install on your own Cloudflare account with one tap, with Get configs and the combine assistant, and the store updates them straight from their developers' releases. Both are installed with random passwords and paths, not the defaults everybody knows. The store no longer mistakes Netra for BPB.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A new panel in Cloud: Spider",
                            "SpiderPanel's Worker, straight from the developer's GitHub, installs on your own Cloudflare account with one tap, and the app is its panel. Only what the other panels lack came over: a concurrent-IP limit per user, and an exit raced among several of your own SOCKS5 or HTTP proxies, the fastest for the user's country and data centre, with health checks and each exit's live state. Users with quota and days and link copy are there too, and like the other panels a \"Get configs\" button sits right in the Cloud tab, followed by the combine-with-clean-IP offer. A new user shows in the list at once.\n\nThe store asks the developer's GitHub for new versions of its Worker and carries the panel's key and address to the new code.\n\nMeasured on a phone: install, a user and a connection worked, 8.6 Mbit/s down. With no exit, sites that are themselves behind Cloudflare do not open, because a Worker cannot connect to Cloudflare's own addresses; the panel page says so.",
                            Icons.Default.Hub
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Gateway: an offline list, no waiting",
                            "The gateway screen no longer goes online on its own and opens at once from the offline list: the last one you fetched, or the fresh list shipped with the app on a first install. Its age is shown beside it, and \"Update list\" fetches a new one whenever you want, as on Windows.\n\nThe update itself is faster, 56 to 17 s on a phone: a route whose name leads to the filter's block page is dropped at once, and the secure lookup goes to a numeric address.",
                            Icons.Default.CloudOff
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "GitHub Tunnel: step-by-step setup",
                            "Setup is three steps in a row and the big button always does the next one: 1) Cloudflare (connect an account first if the Cloud tab has none; otherwise the Worker is installed on it), 2) GitHub, 3) connect. Exit country, rules and accounts appear once setup is done.",
                            Icons.Default.Checklist
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A failed connection now says why",
                            "Every tunnel screen went back to \"ready\" after a failure and hid the reason. It now keeps \"could not connect\" and the reason in place.\n\nIn WARP, when making a WARP account is filtered on your connection, the \"make the identity through a Worker and connect\" button appears right there. Measured on a phone: the filter recognises the WARP account server's name even when it is cut into pieces, so when a Worker exists it is now tried before the disguised route. Cloudflare sometimes rate-limits registration through Workers for a few minutes (error 1015); it is then asked once more, and the error says so.\n\nMeasured on a phone: the account was made through the Worker, connected 38 s after the tap, Cloudflare answered \"warp=on\", 40 Mbit/s down, no leak.",
                            Icons.Default.Info
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A Tools folder on the home screen",
                            "Fixed IP, Sub link, LAN sharing, Usage and Tutorials are gathered in a Tools folder. The home screen now has folders: hold an icon and drop it on another to make one. Inside a folder you can rename it, reorder its icons or drag one out.",
                            Icons.Default.Folder
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The same icons as Windows",
                            "Features present in both apps now use the Windows app's icons. Psiphon keeps its own.",
                            Icons.Default.Palette
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "\"Vercel tunnel\" removed",
                            "Its server had stopped working and the option only broke requests. If you had switched it on, subscriptions, Cloud and Config Studio now work directly.",
                            Icons.Default.Delete
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Config Studio: steadier, faster connections",
                            "Configs no longer keep dropping. A connection starts sooner because it no longer waits on the database, and the connect timeout is longer. IPv6 addresses are supported, and DNS answers faster and in parallel.\n\n**To get these fixes, update the engine on each account from More › Cloudflare accounts.**",
                            Icons.Default.Speed
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Multi-location that works and stays put",
                            "Each country config gets its own fixed, tested exit server and gives the same country on every connection. Every server's country is measured before it is used, and if one stops working it is swapped for a healthy one in the same country. Public servers are used only when they really leave from that country.\n\nThe ports you choose for a person now really apply to their link, and the Locations page has a ready command for running your own exit server on any VPS.",
                            Icons.Default.Public
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Pick the protocols when you create someone: VLESS and Trojan",
                            "When you create a user (one or many) or edit their locations, choose one protocol or both; both run over WebSocket. Afterwards the page lists exactly what was made: each config's protocol, country and exit address.\n\n**XHTTP is paused:** on a workers.dev address Cloudflare stops it from working (measured on a real account). Existing XHTTP configs stay in the list but are left out of subscriptions, so nobody gets a link that cannot connect.",
                            Icons.Default.Layers
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Device limits are really applied",
                            "The \"devices at once\" number is now enforced: while that many devices are connected, a new one is refused. A phone that moves between Wi-Fi and mobile data gets back in within a minute or two.\n\nEach person's page shows how many devices are connected now, and each account's page says whether device limits are active there. The \"recorded but not enforced yet\" text is gone.",
                            Icons.Default.Devices
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Exact, consistent usage",
                            "A person's usage reaches the panel within about a minute and a half; before, it sometimes arrived only after they disconnected. Per-person stats now match their main volume, a 100 MB user stops at about 100 MB, and figures are rounded the same way everywhere.\n\nThe phone's own data meter reads a little higher, because it also counts encryption overhead.",
                            Icons.Default.DataUsage
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "A redesigned Config Studio",
                            "Config Studio has an iOS-style redesign: a bottom tab bar (Home, Users, Stats, More), one consistent icon set instead of emoji, and each thing's state as a colour and a short sentence. Settings open from the gear on Home.",
                            Icons.Default.Palette
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Pull down to refresh",
                            "On every Config Studio page (users, stats, configs, locations, accounts and the rest), pulling the page down reloads its figures.",
                            Icons.Default.Refresh
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "The Cloud section's MLM panel and Config Studio are one",
                            "Both are one engine and one database on each account. On accounts that have Config Studio, updating from the Cloud section now runs Config Studio's own installer (before, it broke subscription links and device limits), \"Users\" opens Config Studio, and \"Remove\" says plainly that it removes Config Studio's engine too. Online status, switching people on and off, and deleted users now agree between the two.",
                            Icons.Default.Sync
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Volume and time left, inside the VPN app itself",
                            "Each subscription now starts with entries that state that person's volume and time left, such as \"Volume left: 874 MB of 1 GB\" and \"Time left: 30 days\". Being ordinary entries, they show in v2rayNG and every other app, and every subscription update works them out from the person's account.\n\nIn this app the same figures show as a card above the subscription's group, for any subscription that sends them, other panels included. Days are counted the same way everywhere: a 30-day subscription reads 30 on its first day.",
                            Icons.Default.DataUsage
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Bug fixes",
                            "Several reported problems are fixed, including: typing 0 in a bulk limit change really removes the limit, a network error is no longer shown as \"not enforced\", adding a config to many people asks first, someone with less than a day left is no longer shown as expired, one phone no longer counts as two devices, and every refused connection is named in Config Studio.",
                            Icons.Default.BugReport
                        ),
                    )
                ),
                ChangelogVersion(
                    "Version 1.2.35",
                    listOf(
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "GitHub Tunnel on Android: your own cloud server on GitHub, through your own Cloudflare relay",
                            "The same system as the Windows app, complete on the phone. One button starts a cloud server on **your own GitHub account's allowance**, reached through a Worker on **your own Cloudflare account** over clean IPs — no shared server anywhere in between.\n\n• GitHub sign-in with a device code (no password typed into the app)\n• several accounts, moving on by itself when one runs out\n• seamless renewal: the next session is made ready and swapped in minutes before the end\n• «end session and save allowance», so an idle server stops spending minutes\n\nEach session's details come back **sealed to a one-time key on this phone** and stay sealed in your private repository. Measured on the phone: the session was ready **about 35 seconds** after the button, downloads at **21 to 25 Mbit/s**.",
                            Icons.Default.Cloud
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Exit country: the connection leaves from the country you pick",
                            "The cloud server brings that country's exit up itself — **VPN Gate first, Psiphon if that fails** — and the connection continues on the same tunnel as another user; nothing new runs on the phone. «Maximum speed» is the cloud server's own address.\n\nThe choice is kept, and **every new session starts preparing it the moment it boots**; in testing, four countries were ready 28 seconds after connecting. «What websites see» shows the address as measured **through the tunnel itself**, and the country list is what the server can really offer right now, with server counts.",
                            Icons.Default.Public
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Sites and apps, each from its own country",
                            "Several rules at once — say Instagram from Korea, a few sites from Germany, one app from Japan — with everything else on the main exit.\n\n**Apps can be chosen too:** every app on the phone that can use the network, system ones included, with icons and search. Which app a connection belongs to is **Android's own answer**, not a guess from the site name.\n\nMeasured on the phone, all at once: ip.me from **Korea**, ifconfig.co from **Germany**, Chrome from the **US**, everything else from **Japan**. When a site is in a rule, that rule wins whichever app opens it. Up to five countries.\n\n**One limit to know:** sites behind Cloudflare encrypt their name in Chrome (ECH), so a site rule cannot recognise them; for such a site, use an app rule.",
                            Icons.Default.Apps
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Which servers carry UDP — labelled and measured",
                            "Every country and every exit says **«with UDP»** or **«no UDP»**: VPN Gate exits carry video calls and games from that country too; Psiphon carries no UDP, and on it UDP leaves from the cloud server's own address.\n\nThe «UDP (calls, games)» row is not a guess: it sends one STUN request **through this very tunnel** and shows the address it was really seen from — and says so when that differs from what websites see, or when nothing gets through.",
                            Icons.Default.Call
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "An exit that silently left from the server's own address now repairs itself",
                            "In testing, the Japan exit on the cloud server stayed «ready» while all of its traffic left from **the server's own US address** — the server's health check only asked «does data flow?», never «from where?».\n\n• The server now measures every exit's egress each minute and **rebuilds a leaking one at once** — and stops using that VPN Gate server for the rest of the session\n• The app, too, says so **openly** when it sees traffic leaving from the server's own address and asks for the rebuild; in testing, back in Japan within 28 seconds\n\nThe server-side fix covers the Windows app as well.",
                            Icons.Default.Security
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Persian alphabetical order in the country lists",
                            "«ژاپن», «کره» and «کانادا» came after «ویتنام», because the list was sorted by character code rather than the Persian alphabet. It now follows the language's own collation.",
                            Icons.Default.SortByAlpha
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Gemini and Google services open on Cloudflare configs",
                            "The «not available in your country» message in Gemini and some Google apps is fixed on Cloudflare configs. It can be switched on or off with one switch in Settings.",
                            Icons.Default.Public
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Identity creation for WireGuard, MASQUE and WARP-in-WARP",
                            "Creating a WARP identity (registration), which was blocked on some networks, works again — for WireGuard, MASQUE and WARP-in-WARP.",
                            Icons.Default.VpnKey
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Config Studio improvements",
                            "Config Studio is faster and more stable, with improvements across its screens.",
                            Icons.Default.Tune
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "Multi-location (early version)",
                            "A first version of multi-location configs in Config Studio. It is still experimental and may not work correctly everywhere.",
                            Icons.Default.Language
                        ),
                        ChangelogItem(
                            "More accurate usage counting",
                            "Users' data usage is counted and shown more accurately.",
